    "name": "cyboros-test-registry",
    "model": "REDflare-style stable test-ID registry (repo-vet churchofmalware plan QW7)",
    "standards": {
      "wstg": "OWASP WSTG v4.2 category/test ids",
      "asvs": "OWASP ASVS chapters (short name form, pointer-level not claim-level)",
      "cwe": "MITRE CWE ids",
      "owasp_api": "OWASP API Security Top 10 (2023) ids",
      "owasp_llm": "OWASP GenAI LLM Top 10 (2025/2026) ids",
      "owasp_agentic": "OWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications 2026 ids (ASI01-ASI10)",
      "attack": "MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise technique ids; tactic/name resolved in tools/attack-coverage.js",
      "note_2025": "Registry aligned with OWASP Top 10:2025 — A01 Broken Access Control now explicitly covers BOLA/BFLA (bola/bfla classes); new 2025 categories A03 Software Supply Chain (supply-chain) and A10 Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions (exceptional); plus the 2025/2026 GenAI surface (llm, mcp).",
      "note_2026-10": "Added three classes on 2026-10-18 after the RAG/vuln-DB review: cspt (client-side path traversal → CSRF chain, Doyensec CSPT-to-CSRF), data-api (Supabase/PostgREST RLS+grants, Firebase rules — configuration class, no CVE), h2-desync (HTTP/2→HTTP/1.1 downgrade, H2.CL/H2.TE, cache poisoning via desync; PortSwigger 2025). coverage.js now DERIVES its class list from this registry, keeping the five historical display names as aliases."
    },
    "note": "Pointers to methodology references per finding/vuln CLASS. They guide the tester and enrich reports; they are NOT evidence that a check was executed."
  },
